### Warehouse Inventory API Test Suite
### Make sure your server is running at http://localhost:3000

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. GET all inventory items
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory

### 2. GET inventory statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory/stats

### 3. GET a specific inventory item by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory/1

### 4. GET low stock items
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory/low-stock

### 5. GET items by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory/category/Electronics

### 6. POST - Create a new inventory item
POST {{baseUrl}}/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wireless Mouse - Logitech MX Master 3",
  "sku": "LG-MX3-001",
  "quantity": 25,
  "location": "A-15-2",
  "category": "Electronics",
  "minStock": 10,
  "maxStock": 100,
  "unit": "units",
  "supplier": "Logitech Inc."
}

### 7. PUT - Update an existing inventory item
PUT {{baseUrl}}/inventory/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 50,
  "location": "A-12-5"
}

### 8. PATCH - Adjust inventory quantity (add stock)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/inventory/1/quantity
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "adjustment": 10,
  "operation": "add"
}

### 9. PATCH - Adjust inventory quantity (subtract stock)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/inventory/1/quantity
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "adjustment": 5,
  "operation": "subtract"
}

### 10. DELETE - Delete an inventory item
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/inventory/2

### 11. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 12. GET all inventory items after operations
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory
